{"kind":"request","text":"Bound resident memory growth with sequence depth.","body":{"conditions":"Measured at main 316d5aeb (docs/reference/performance.md): resident RSS grows about 31 KB per record across harness depths 100 to 1,000, and the live resident holds 347 MiB at 5,786 records. That extrapolates to about 1.55 GB at PREVIEW's 50,000 records against a 1 GiB target, and about 15.5 GB at FIRST-PRODUCTION's 500,000 against 4 GiB; both miss. Suspected bounding component: the projection retains all application events in memory. Satisfied when a resident serving 50,000 records stays under 1 GiB peak RSS, with the per-record slope re-measured and reported.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}